NAME
       popen, pclose, system - run a command

SYNOPSIS
       #include <stdio.h>
       #include <stdlib.h>

       FILE *popen(const char *cmd, const char *mode);
       int   pclose(FILE *f);
       int   system(const char *cmd);

DESCRIPTION
       popen runs CMD through the shell with a pipe attached: mode "r"
       reads what the command writes, mode "w" feeds it input. pclose
       waits for the command and returns its exit status.

       system runs CMD and waits, with input and output inherited.

       CMD goes to the shell, so anything interpolated into it is
       interpreted. Build the string from values you control, or use
       fork and execve directly.

RETURN VALUE
       popen returns a stream or NULL; pclose and system return the
       command's exit status, or -1.

SEE ALSO
       fork(2), execve(2), pipe(2), stdio(3), csh(1)
